From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:08:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] minigbm-upstream: gbm_mesa: Pad NV12 encoder input to
 macroblocks

Hardware encoders work on whole 16x16 macroblocks: they may read the rows
up to the next multiple of 16 and a little past the chroma plane. A
1080p NV12 buffer is 3110400 bytes, while the Exynos MFC reads 3133696.
Reserve those rows and one page in NV12 and NV21 buffers allocated for an
encoder, so that these reads do not fault in the IOMMU. The plane layout
does not change.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I48e74e7e071a9f0cfc991316932b2cde25c076d7
---
 gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
index 5ff0f86..af092b8 100644
--- a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
+++ b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
@@ -378,6 +378,15 @@ int gbm_mesa_bo_create(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t
 		/* Always use linear for spoofed format allocations. */
 		drv_bo_from_format(bo, alloc_args.width, 1, alloc_args.height, format);
 		bo_layout_ready = true;
+		/* Encoders work on whole 16x16 macroblocks: they may read the
+		 * rows up to the next multiple of 16 and a little past the
+		 * chroma plane, and a read outside the buffer is an IOMMU fault.
+		 * Reserve those rows and one page. */
+		if ((format == DRM_FORMAT_NV12 || format == DRM_FORMAT_NV21) &&
+		    (use_flags & BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER)) {
+			uint32_t rows = ALIGN(alloc_args.height, 16) - alloc_args.height;
+			bo->meta.total_size += alloc_args.width * rows * 3 / 2 + 4096;
+		}
 		bo->meta.total_size = ALIGN(bo->meta.total_size, size_align);
 		alloc_args.drm_format = DRM_FORMAT_R8;
 		alloc_args.width = bo->meta.total_size;
